{
  "meta": {
    "title": "APEC EBT Dashboard — Data Visualization Colors",
    "description": "Colors currently used across the APEC EBT dashboard, grouped by what they represent: fuels, sectors (consumption end-use), regions, and economies. Within each category, a 'standard'/base list is the single source of truth for hex values; where the dashboard merges multiple raw codes into one display label, that entry carries an 'inherits_from' (or 'members') pointer back to the base list instead of repeating the hex.",
    "sources": [
      "apec-ebt-dashboard/src/data_io/egeda_ebt_utils.py (ebt_colors, fuel_color_assign_set1, sector_color_assign_set1, region_color_assign_set1)",
      "apec-ebt-dashboard/src/data_io/aggregation_rules.py (fuel_groupings, fuel_group_types*, regex_groups_flows_type_tfc/tfec, regions_analysis)",
      "apec-ebt-dashboard/src/plots/apec_palette.py (economy hue-family + lightness addressing)"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "When Oil is disaggregated into individual products, the remaining products grouped under 'Other Oil' keep Oil's original color; Diesel takes the separate oil-products color.",
      "When Solar and Wind merge into 'Solar & Wind', the combined label takes Solar's color.",
      "LPG and Wind use closely the same color. Since the chance of these two appearing on the same chart is small, reusing the color is acceptable.",
      "AvGas and FuelOil use closely the same colors as Hydro and Geothermal respectively. Since the chance of these appearing on the same chart is small, reusing the colors is acceptable."
    ]
  },

